 :what-was-built
 {:where "checks/library_graph_lint.clj"
  :flag "--posthoc-warrant store|pattern-text, else LIBRARY_POSTHOC_WARRANT, default :store"
  :default-unchanged
  "The default arm is the bar exactly as it stood, so every previously recorded
   number is still comparable. Confirmed: the C88 pin reads 1247 files and
   {:why 86 :why-posthoc 0 :how 27 :see-also 141} before and after the change,
   and war-room/aif :store runs on the untouched library are byte-identical to
   slices 1 and 2 (/tmp/L9s3gates/before-*-store.edn)."
  :fail-closed
  "A pattern-text warrant resolves against the library, not the store: the
   excerpt must occur in the ONE line window the record names. A window that
   runs off the end, a missing file, or an excerpt that sits elsewhere in the
   same file are all :pattern-text-excerpt-mismatch."
  :lane-boundary
  "Admissible only on a :why-posthoc edge and only on that arm. An authored @why
   carrying a pattern-text warrant is :malformed-attestation even under the
   flag, and a pattern-text row carrying a store :id is refused, so the
   harvested lane's bar (P-validated-R5 law O2) is untouched by this change."
  :tests "test/library_graph_lint_test.clj:302 an-authored-warrant-is-refused-by-the-store-bar-and-verified-under-its-own-arm -- 13 tests / 143 assertions overall, was 12 / 125"}

